  <img decoding="async" width="696" height="392" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/s2fcover-768x432-1.jpg" class="attachment-medium_large size-medium_large wp-post-image" alt="" loading="lazy" style="float:left; margin:0 15px 15px 0;" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/s2fcover-768x432-1.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/s2fcover-300x169.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/s2fcover-1024x576.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/s2fcover-696x392.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/s2fcover-1068x601.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/s2fcover-747x420.jpg 747w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/s2fcover-190x107.jpg 190w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/s2fcover-380x214.jpg 380w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/s2fcover-760x428.jpg 760w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/s2fcover.jpg 1280w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 696px) 100vw, 696px" /></p> 
  
  <p>
    <strong>The leading cryptocurrency bitcoin has dropped 20% in value after Tesla announced on May 12, the electric car firm would not be accepting bitcoin for purchases. Two days later, the creator of the notorious stock-to-flow cross-asset (S2FX) price model, Plan B, shared his model and said the S2FX was still “intact.” Plan B still shows confidence in the bitcoin bull run and expects another 5x in the next six months.</strong>
  </p>
  
  <h2 style="text-align: center;">
    S2FX Price Model Still ‘Intact’
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    Despite the recent crypto market downturn, Plan B still seems positive that the bitcoin bull run is not quite over. “Plan B,” is a pseudonym leveraged by the Twitter account @100trillionusd and also the creator of the popular stock-to-flow (S2F) price model. This particular model leverages a ratio of bitcoin’s scarcity (BTC in circulation) to BTC issuance. At the time of writing, the Bitcoin network’s inflation rate per annum is approximately 1.77% and will continue to drop lower as time passes.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    Plan B first published his paper called “Modeling Bitcoin Value with Scarcity” on March 22, 2019. The stock-to-flow model or S2F, quantifies scarcity similar to assets like gold and silver. It takes the BTC in circulation and divides it by the annual issuance rate. When Plan B published that paper, bitcoin (BTC) had a market capitalization of $70 billion and today, the market valuation is $844 billion. Moreover, Plan B has updated the S2F model and now calls it the “BTC S2F cross-asset (S2FX) model.”
  </p>
  
  <p>
    “S2FX model enables valuation of different assets like silver, gold and BTC with one formula,” Plan B S2FX description explains.
  </p><figure id="attachment_459692" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-459692" style="width: 1200px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
  <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="wp-image-459692 size-full" title="Bitcoin Stock-to-Flow Still 'Intact' Says Creator, Crypto Fear Index Taps 12-Month Low" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/e1wudvgxmaunorj.png" alt="Bitcoin Stock-to-Flow Still 'Intact' Says Creator, Crypto Fear Index Taps 12-Month Low" width="1200" height="665" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/e1wudvgxmaunorj.png 1200w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/e1wudvgxmaunorj-300x166.png 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/e1wudvgxmaunorj-1024x567.png 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/e1wudvgxmaunorj-768x426.png 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/e1wudvgxmaunorj-696x385.png 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/e1wudvgxmaunorj-1068x592.png 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/e1wudvgxmaunorj-758x420.png 758w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-459692" class="wp-caption-text">Plan B’s latest S2FX chart shared on May 14, 2021.</figcaption></figure> 
  
  <p>
    The day after Tesla announced it was not accepting BTC for purchases, Plan B took to Twitter sharing an S2FX chart and said: “S2FX intact … this is starting to look like 2013 bull market.” The following day Plan B shared another chart and gave his 467,000 Twitter followers another S2FX update:
  </p>
  
  <blockquote>
    <p>
      <em><strong>Net result (after Turkey ban, US tax FUD, Faketoshi law suits, Elon/Tesla energy FUD) is that bitcoin is 5x higher than ~6 months ago. And both S2FX model + onchain data indicate that we are only halfway this bull market. I would not be surprised to see another 5x next ~6 months.</strong></em>
    </p>
  </blockquote>
  
  <p>
    <!-- growjs zone placement 31 -->
    
    <ins> <ins class="growjs-placement"></ins> </ins> <!-- end of growjs zone placement -->
  </p>
  
  <h2 style="text-align: center;">
    Crypto Fear & Greed Index Hits a 1 Year Low, Momentum Indicator Indicates ‘Typical Mid-Bull-Cycle Drop’ Says Plan B
  </h2>
  
  <p>
    Furthermore, on May 17, the Crypto Fear & Greed Index (CFGI) shows a score of 27 pointing to “fear” and sentiment is the same as it was over a year ago today.
  </p><figure id="attachment_459693" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-459693" style="width: 1300px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
  <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="wp-image-459693 size-full" title="Bitcoin Stock-to-Flow Still 'Intact' Says Creator, Crypto Fear Index Taps 12-Month Low" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/greedfear66ffg.jpg" alt="Bitcoin Stock-to-Flow Still 'Intact' Says Creator, Crypto Fear Index Taps 12-Month Low" width="1300" height="500" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/greedfear66ffg.jpg 1300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/greedfear66ffg-300x115.jpg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/greedfear66ffg-1024x394.jpg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/greedfear66ffg-768x295.jpg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/greedfear66ffg-696x268.jpg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/greedfear66ffg-1068x411.jpg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/greedfear66ffg-1092x420.jpg 1092w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1300px) 100vw, 1300px" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-459693" class="wp-caption-text">CFGI data on May 17, 2021.</figcaption></figure> 
  
  <p>
    The index, a metric that “analyzes the emotions and sentiments from different sources and crunches them into one simple number,” reached this same region on April 28, 2020. 30 days ago, CFGI data shows that the sentiment analysis was “extreme greed” or a score of 76. Seven-day statistics show that the CFGI score was 72 or “greed.”
  </p><figure id="attachment_459691" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-459691" style="width: 1200px" class="wp-caption aligncenter">
  
  <img decoding="async" loading="lazy" class="wp-image-459691 size-full" title="Bitcoin Stock-to-Flow Still 'Intact' Says Creator, Crypto Fear Index Taps 12-Month Low" src="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/e1b1qn2x0aun3ec.jpeg" alt="Bitcoin Stock-to-Flow Still 'Intact' Says Creator, Crypto Fear Index Taps 12-Month Low" width="1200" height="675" srcset="https://technologymanias.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/e1b1qn2x0aun3ec.jpeg 1200w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/e1b1qn2x0aun3ec-300x169.jpeg 300w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/e1b1qn2x0aun3ec-1024x576.jpeg 1024w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/e1b1qn2x0aun3ec-768x432.jpeg 768w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/e1b1qn2x0aun3ec-696x392.jpeg 696w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/e1b1qn2x0aun3ec-1068x601.jpeg 1068w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/e1b1qn2x0aun3ec-747x420.jpeg 747w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/e1b1qn2x0aun3ec-190x107.jpeg 190w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/e1b1qn2x0aun3ec-380x214.jpeg 380w, https://news.bitcoin.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/05/e1b1qn2x0aun3ec-760x428.jpeg 760w" sizes="auto, (max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" /><figcaption id="caption-attachment-459691" class="wp-caption-text">Bitcoin’s Relative Strength Index (RSI) chart shared by Plan B on May 15, 2021.</figcaption></figure> 
  
  <p>
    On Saturday, Plan B discussed bitcoin’s Relative Strength Index (RSI) and his thoughts on the next few months. The technical analysis tool dubbed the “Relative Strength Index” (RSI) is essentially a momentum indicator that can help analysts define oversold or overbought conditions in a market.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    “Bitcoin relative strength index (RSI),” Plan B said sharing another chart. “We are at the typical mid-bull-cycle drop in RSI (yellow circles), in between 2013 and 2017. Excited about [the] next couple of months,” Plan B added.
  </p>
  
  <p>
    <em><strong>What do you think about Plan B’s current market assessment? Let us know what you think about this subject in the comments section below. </strong></em>
  </p>
